2. Proprietary. The Business Code is proprietary. It is published so that
   customers can read and audit it; publication grants no licence.

3. Use. You may use, copy and modify the Business Code only:
   (a) in production, while you hold a valid Dueproof Business licence for
       the organisation using it, and only for the features and term that
       licence lists; or
   (b) to develop and test Dueproof itself, without production use.

4. Restrictions. You may not:
   (a) remove, disable or circumvent the licence check, or alter it so that
       a feature works without a valid licence that lists it;
   (b) sell, sublicense, rent, host for others or otherwise distribute the
       Business Code, alone or as part of another product or service;
   (c) use the Business Code to build a product or service that competes
       with Dueproof.

5. Licence keys. Licence files are issued by Dueproof and signed with
   Dueproof's key. A licence file is personal to the licensee named in it
   and may not be shared.

6. Contributions. Contributions to the Business Code are accepted only
